    pr_ref:  # 5a5b
    description: "INV-fahub Scala facet. scala.py misbinds an unresolvable-receiver call (e.g. x.copy()) to an arbitrary same-named internal def: Record.copy @0.68 (= 0.80 base x 0.85 suffix). Misbind sites: scala.py:853-864 (local_symbols bare bind @0.85 — methods registered under both short+qualified name at 498-499) and scala.py:865-890 (resolver.lookup bare bind @0.68). Root cause: when receiver_name is present but NOT in var_types, edge_added stays False and the receiver is silently dropped -> bare short-name binds (treats x.copy() like bare copy()).\n\nFIX (atomic, INV-nilud-conform; mirrors WI-noham Part A / py.py): when a receiver is present but its type is unresolvable, emit py.py's unresolved shape instead of the bare-name bind — edge_type=calls, dst=scala:external:0-0:{name}:unresolved, is_resolved=False, evidence_type=ast_call (-> 0.40 derived per ADR-0039), meta={call_construct:method, + receiver_type_hint when a type is establishable}. THREAD annotated vals (val x: Foo = f(), currently dropped — only params + `val x = new Foo()` tracked) into var_types so a typed receiver still resolves (recall recovery: the hint the shared inherited_calls linker Site-2 Step-1 consumes). ADD 'scala' to the inherited_calls Site-2 language set for Step-1 direct (method-on-typed-receiver) resolution. Defer the Scala trait-linearization MRO walker (_walk_linearization, marked FUTURE in inherited_calls.py) to a later incremental PR (as Python deferred its C3 walker).\n\nTests: test_inherited_calls_linker.py template (swap lang=scala) + a scala.py producer test (untyped/duck receiver -> no hint -> external unresolved; annotated-val receiver -> resolves). Blast radius: scala.py leaf + one linker Site-2 lang-set entry; no CORE resolver change. Recall-regression severity: MODERATE. Reproduces on current code (verified 2026-07-17)."  # 5a5b
    fields: {}  # 5a5b
